<title>POLAND: Preliminary Polish bond auction offers for Q1 1997.</title>
<headline>Preliminary Polish bond auction offers for Q1 1997.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Finance Ministry has released the preliminary amounts of bonds to be offered in addition at primary tenders in the first quarter of 1997, the treasury's public debt department said in a statement.</p>
<p>NOTE. In the bond symbol in brackets, the first two letters denote the type of bond, the following two digits are the month of maturity and the last two digits the year of maturity of the particular issue.</p>
<p>The actual amount of bonds on offer is announced a week before the tender.@</p>
<p>    DATE		   BOND TYPE			  BOND SYMBOL</p>
<p> Jan 14	   - floating 10-yr bond tender	     (DZ0107)</p>
<p>AMOUNT (PLN million) - 600</p>
<p> Jan 16	   - fixed 2-yr, 5-yr bond tender  (OS0299,OS0202)</p>
<p>AMOUNT (PLN million) - 700</p>
<p> Jan 20-Feb 2   - index-linked 1-yr bond subscription  (IR0398)</p>
<p>AMOUNT (PLN million) - 400</p>
<p> Jan 21	   - floating three-year bond tender	(TZ0200)</p>
<p>AMOUNT (PLN million) - 700@</p>
<p>  Jan 28	   - index-linked 1-yr bond tender	 *(RP0398)</p>
<p>AMOUNT (PLN million) - 200</p>
<p> Feb 3-April 30 - floating 3-yr bond public sale	 (TZ0200)</p>
<p>AMOUNT (PLN million) - 400</p>
<p> Feb 5	    - fixed 2-yr, 5-yr bond tender  (ASO699,OSO602)</p>
<p>AMOUNT (PLN million) - 800</p>
<p> Feb 20	   - fixed 5-yr bond tender (assimilated) (OS0601)</p>
<p>AMOUNT (PLN million) - 200</p>
<p> Feb 25	   - index-linked 1-yr bond tender	 *(RP0398)</p>
<p>AMOUNT (PLN million) - 200@</p>
<p>March 3-May 28 - index-linked 1-yr bond public sale **(IR0398)</p>
<p>AMOUNT (PLN million) - max 400</p>
<p> March 11	 - floating 10-yr bond tender    (DZ0406,DZ0407)</p>
<p>AMOUNT (PLN million) - 600</p>
<p> March 20	 - fixed 5-yr bond tender (assimilated) (OS0601)</p>
<p>AMOUNT (PLN million) - 200</p>
<p>* Index-linked one-year bond issues of the IR series are for the public and carry interest of 300 basis points above year-on-year inflation two months before maturity.@</p>
<p>The RP series of one-year bonds is sold at primary tenders for institutions and does not have the 300 basis point margin above inflation in its interest mechanism.</p>
<p>The five-year assimilated bonds and the DZ0406 10-year bond are from unsold 1996 issues.</p>
<p>** The rest of unsold bonds from index-linked 1-yr bond subscription  (IR0398)</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
